Feature: Core metronome
  As a musician using the metronome TUI
  I want to control tempo and start/stop the beat
  So that I can practice at a steady click

  Background:
    Given the metronome app has started

  @ft:1
  Scenario: Default BPM on startup
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    And   the status bar should show "STOPPED"
    And   the status bar should show the app name "mn"

  @ft:2
  Scenario: Start the metronome
    When  I press "space"
    Then  the status bar should show "PLAYING"

  @ft:3
  Scenario: Stop the metronome
    Given the metronome is playing
    When  I press "space"
    Then  the status bar should show "STOPPED"

  @ft:4
  Scenario: Increase BPM by a small increment
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "up"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 121 BPM"

  @ft:5
  Scenario: Decrease BPM by a small increment
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "down"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 119 BPM"

  @ft:6
  Scenario: Increase BPM by a large increment
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "shift+up"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

  @ft:7
  Scenario: Decrease BPM by a large increment
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "shift+down"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 110 BPM"

  @ft:8
  Scenario: BPM cannot go below the minimum
    Given the BPM is 20
    When  I press "down"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 20 BPM"

  @ft:9
  Scenario: BPM cannot go above the maximum
    Given the BPM is 300
    When  I press "up"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 300 BPM"

  @ft:10
  Scenario: Beat pulse visualization advances on each beat and wraps after beat 4
    Given the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  beat 1 of the measure is struck
    Then  only the beat 1 dot should be lit
    And   beat slots 2, 3, and 4 should be unlit
    When  beat 2 is struck
    Then  only the beat 2 dot should be lit
    And   the beat 1 dot should return to its unlit state
    When  beat 3 is struck
    Then  only the beat 3 dot should be lit
    When  beat 4 is struck
    Then  only the beat 4 dot should be lit
    And   beat slots 1, 2, and 3 should be unlit
    When  the next beat is struck
    Then  the lit dot should jump back to beat 1, not advance to a fifth slot

  @ft:11
  Scenario: Beat 1 of each measure is visually accented
    Given the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  a new measure begins
    Then  a "^" caret should be shown above beat 1's dot
    And   beat 1's dot should pulse in the accent color when struck
    And   beats 2 through 4 should show no caret and pulse in the plain color when struck

  @ft:12
  Scenario: j mirrors the down key for BPM
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "j"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 119 BPM"

  @ft:13
  Scenario: k mirrors the up key for BPM
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "k"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 121 BPM"

  @ft:14
  Scenario: shift+j mirrors the shift+down key for BPM
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "shift+j"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 110 BPM"

  @ft:15
  Scenario: shift+k mirrors the shift+up key for BPM
    Given the BPM is 120
    When  I press "shift+k"
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

